{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2513"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of steam generators, except central heating hot water boilers"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2513"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :steam-generator/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :pressure-vessel-safety :boiler-explosion-safety :equipment-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :steam-generator-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "SteamGeneratorAdvisor ⊣ Steam Generator Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for industrial-scale steam-generator/boiler
 manufacturing (fabrication/welding/pressure-vessel-assembly/hydrotest
 lines producing finished fire-tube boilers, water-tube boilers,
 waste-heat-recovery boilers and heat-recovery steam generators --
 excluding central heating hot water boilers, which this class
 explicitly excludes) -- not direct fabrication-line-equipment control
 authority and not pressure-vessel-safety-certification authority (e.g.
 ASME Boiler and Pressure Vessel Code (BPVC) Section I 'S' stamp
 certification or National Board of Boiler and Pressure Vessel
 Inspectors (NBBI) registration). Four ops (`:log-production-batch` /
 `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Twelve concrete
 governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD invariants:
 propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect
 allowlist (no direct fabrication-line-equipment control), permanent
 equipment-actuate block, permanent pressure-vessel-safety-
 certification-authority block (this actor never self-issues an ASME
 BPVC 'S' stamp or National Board registration), independent equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-quantity recompute against the batch's own
 logged production quantity, double-schedule guard, product-type
 validation, hydrotest-pressure plausibility validation, and
 defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging
 (equipment-safety/pressure-vessel-safety concern) ALWAYS escalates to
 a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the only op
 eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
